 r←{req}Stats nums;n;s;mean
⍝ POST /Stats   body: [2,4,4,4,5,5,7,9]
⍝   →  {"count":8,"max":9,"mean":5,"median":4.5,"min":2,"sd":2}
⍝ An ambivalent tradfn: Jarvis passes its request object as the left
⍝ argument, which we use to answer 400 Bad Request for bad input. Tests
⍝ can call it with no left argument.
 r←⎕NS ⍬
 :If ~(1=≢⍴nums)∧(0<≢nums)∧{0::0 ⋄ ∧/⍵=⍵+0}nums
     :If 0≠⎕NC'req' ⋄ req.Fail 400 ⋄ :EndIf
     r.error←'send a non-empty list of numbers, e.g. [1,2,3]'
     :Return
 :EndIf
 n←≢nums
 s←nums[⍋nums]
 mean←(+/nums)÷n
 r.count←n
 r.mean←mean
 r.median←(+/s[(⌈n÷2),1+⌊n÷2])÷2
 r.min←⌊/nums
 r.max←⌈/nums
 r.sd←((+/(nums-mean)*2)÷n)*0.5          ⍝ population standard deviation
